# Copy this file to client/.env (gitignored, checkout-local) for local
# development, and uncomment whichever settings you need. An unset value
# keeps the default behavior. On Netlify the two VITE_SUPABASE_* values are
# site environment variables instead (docs/DEPLOY.md step 7), read at build
# time; the dev-server settings aren't used there.
# Every variable the client and its Vite config read is listed here
# (docs/architecture/LLD.md §9).

# Supabase Auth (docs/architecture/LLD.md §6, §9): the project URL and its
# public key, both safe to ship in the bundle. Required: without them the
# sign-in screen only says sign-in isn't configured. Built into the bundle,
# so changing either needs a rebuild. Local stack: `npx supabase status`
# prints both (URL http://127.0.0.1:54321). A hosted project shows them under
# Project Settings > API Keys: the publishable key or the legacy anon key.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon or publishable key>

# Vite dev server only. Only needed to run a second checkout alongside
# another one: see server/.env.example and README's "Running a second
# checkout alongside an existing one". VITE_DEV_PORT defaults to 5173
# (scripts/kill-ports.js reads it too). VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET is where the
# dev server sends /api, default http://localhost:4000, so it must match
# server/.env's PORT, otherwise this checkout's client silently talks to
# another checkout's server.
# VITE_DEV_PORT=5273
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:4100

# GitHub storage build only (`vite build --mode github`); the Supabase build
# ignores it. The sections a new ledger starts with ticked, with
# ENABLED_MODULES's rules (docs/architecture/LLD.md §9): comma-separated,
# unset means all. A fork for one purpose can ship "expenses" here.
# VITE_DEFAULT_MODULES=expenses

# GitHub storage build only, and optional: "Sign in with GitHub" (#10,
# signin-helper/README.md). Set all three to show the button; with any one
# missing or blank the build has no button and no helper URL, and token
# paste works as before. All public (the client secret lives only in the
# helper), so in CI they are Actions variables, not secrets. The Supabase
# build ignores them.
# VITE_GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=<the GitHub App's client ID>
# VITE_GITHUB_APP_SLUG=<the App's URL name, as in github.com/apps/<slug>>
# VITE_GITHUB_SIGNIN_HELPER_URL=https://ledger-signin-helper.<subdomain>.workers.dev
